From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheKit <thekit@disroot.org>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:24:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] base: Hide the system bars and app decorations in per-app
 host windows

A per-app host window is composed from one task's layers, so the system bars
and the app handle never reach it. They only take space from the app, and the
window swallows touches meant for it, so claim nothing while the host is in
that mode.

The back gesture stays: EdgeBackGestureHandler watches the display rather
than the navigation bar window, so an edge swipe still goes back inside a
per-app window. That needs gesture navigation; three-button mode leaves one
with no way back until the host sends one.

The mode arrives in the per_app_host_windows setting, published by the
Waydroid platform service. Nothing here reads waydroid properties.

Change-Id: I02a0d51709a2bd3a122f712f9d390984254e270f
